The audit now has a clear shape: most of Grok’s structural/corpus criticisms are confirmed; Agy’s p. 248 “major MISS” is not. Lem rejects an electronic imitation of a whole human nervous system there, while the cited 2026 systems neither match that object nor yet produce theories in Lem’s strict p. 243 sense. The cleaner negative is the formal-substrate bet at pp. 251/263.
